      "text": "Whiskey production began in Ireland and Scotland in the late 15th century, with the first written record of whiskey production dating to 1496.",
      "date": "1496"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Gin Craze in England",
      "text": "In the early 18th century, gin became extremely popular in England, leading to the 'Gin Craze,' a period of excessive consumption and social issues.",
      "date": "1700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Prohibition in the United States",
      "text": "The 18th Amendment to the United States Constitution, enacted in 1920, prohibited the manufacture, sale, and transportation of alcoholic beverages, including liquor. This period lasted until 1933.",
      "date": "1920"
