      "text": "In 1986, Huey Lewis and the News released their fourth album, 'Fore!,' which included hits like 'Stuck with You' and 'Hip to Be Square.' The album reached number one on the Billboard 200.",
      "date": "1986"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Grammy Award for Best Music Video",
      "text": "In 1986, the band won a Grammy Award for Best Music Video, Long Form for 'The Heart of Rock 'n' Roll.'",
      "date": "1986"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Small World'",
      "text": "The band released their fifth studio album, 'Small World,' in 1988. While it did not achieve the same level of success as previous albums, it still reached the top 20 on the Billboard 200.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Hard at Play'",
      "text": "In 1991, the band released 'Hard at Play,' which included the hit singles 'Couple Days Off' and 'It Hit Me Like a Hammer.'",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Plan B'",
      "text": "After a hiatus, Huey Lewis and the News released 'Plan B' in 2001, marking their first album of new material in a decade.",
      "date": "2001"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'Soulsville'",
      "text": "In 2010, the band released 'Soulsville,' an album of covers of classic soul songs, recorded at the historic Ardent Studios in Memphis.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Huey Lewis Diagnosed with Meniere's Disease",
      "text": "In 2018, Huey Lewis announced that he had been diagnosed with Meniere's disease, a disorder affecting the inner ear, which led to the cancellation of the band's tour dates.",
      "date": "2018"
    }
  ]
}

