      "headline": "Creation of Roth IRA",
      "text": "The Roth IRA was established by the Taxpayer Relief Act of 1997, named after Senator William Roth of Delaware, who was an advocate for the legislation.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Year Roth IRAs Available",
      "text": "Roth IRAs became available to the public in 1998, allowing individuals to make contributions to this new type of retirement account.",
      "date": "1998"
