      "headline": "U.S. Carrier Strikes on Tulagi",
      "text": "On May 4, 1942, aircraft from the U.S. carrier Yorktown launched attacks on Japanese forces at Tulagi, inflicting damage on Japanese ships and installations.",
      "date": "1942-05-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Carrier Battle Begins",
      "text": "On May 7, 1942, the main carrier battle began with both sides launching airstrikes. The Japanese light carrier Shoho was sunk by U.S. aircraft.",
      "date": "1942-05-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Major Engagements and Losses",
      "text": "On May 8, 1942, both sides suffered significant losses. The U.S. carrier Lexington was severely damaged and later scuttled, while the Japanese carrier Shokaku was heavily damaged.",
      "date": "1942-05-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Battle of the Coral Sea",
      "text": "The battle concluded on May 8, 1942, with both sides withdrawing. It was a strategic victory for the Allies as it halted the Japanese advance on Port Moresby.",
      "date": "1942-05-08"
    }
  ]
}

