      "date": "1954"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cultural Revolution Impact",
      "text": "During the Cultural Revolution (1966-1976), the functions of the NPC were largely suspended as political turmoil affected the governance structure of China.",
      "date": "1966"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Resumption of Regular Sessions",
      "text": "After the end of the Cultural Revolution, the National People's Congress resumed its regular sessions and legislative functions in the late 1970s.",
      "date": "1978"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reforms and Opening Up",
      "text": "In the 1980s, the NPC played a significant role in the reform and opening-up policies initiated by Deng Xiaoping, which transformed China's economy and governance.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Constitutional Amendments",
      "text": "The NPC has been responsible for several constitutional amendments, including those in 1982, 1993, 1999, and 2004, which have shaped the legal and political framework of China.",
      "date": "1982"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Largest Legislative Body",
      "text": "As of 2023, the National People's Congress is the largest legislative body in the world, with 2,977 members.",
      "date": "2023"
    }
  ]
}

