      "headline": "Battle of Buxar",
      "text": "The Battle of Buxar was fought between 22 and 23 October 1764. It was a significant battle between the forces of the British East India Company, under the command of Major Hector Munro, and the combined armies of Balwant Singh, Maharaja of the Banaras State; Mir Qasim, Nawab of Bengal; Shuja-ud-Daula, Nawab of Awadh; and Shah Alam II, Emperor of the Mughal Empire.",
      "date": "1764-10-22"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Outcome of the Battle",
      "text": "The British East India Company emerged victorious in the Battle of Buxar. This victory solidified British control over Bengal and laid the foundation for British dominance in India.",
      "date": "1764-10-23"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Allahabad",
      "text": "Following the Battle of Buxar, the Treaty of Allahabad was signed in 1765. This treaty granted the British East India Company the right to collect revenue in Bengal, Bihar, and Orissa, marking a significant step in the establishment of British rule in India.",
      "date": "1765"
    }
  ]
}

