      "headline": "End of Mycenaean Civilization",
      "text": "The Mycenaean civilization, which dominated the Greek mainland, collapsed around 1100 BCE, marking the beginning of the Greek Dark Ages.",
      "date": "-1100"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Protogeometric Period Begins",
      "text": "Around 1050 BCE, the Protogeometric period began, characterized by the use of geometric motifs in pottery.",
