      "text": "The Greek alphabet was developed during the late Greek Dark Ages, around 800 BCE, influenced by the Phoenician script.",
      "date": "-0800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Emergence of City-States",
      "text": "By the end of the Greek Dark Ages, around 800 BCE, the polis or city-state began to emerge as the dominant political structure in Greece.",
