      "text": "During the 17th century, Roatán became a haven for pirates, including the infamous Henry Morgan, who used the island as a base for raiding Spanish ships.",
      "date": "1600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Occupation",
      "text": "In 1742, the British briefly occupied Roatán, using it as a military base against the Spanish.",
      "date": "1742"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Spanish Reassert Control",
      "text": "In 1782, the Spanish reasserted control over Roatán, expelling the British and establishing a more permanent presence.",
      "date": "1782"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Settlement",
      "text": "In the early 19th century, British settlers, including the Garifuna people, began to settle on Roatán.",
      "date": "1800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ceded to Honduras",
      "text": "In 1859, the British ceded the Bay Islands, including Roatán, to Honduras under the Wyke-Cruz Treaty.",
      "date": "1859"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Municipal Division",
      "text": "Roatán is divided into two municipalities: José Santos Guardiola in the east and Roatán in the west.",
