      "headline": "Topical Formulations",
      "text": "In the years following its introduction, ketoconazole was developed into topical formulations for treating skin infections and conditions like dandruff and seborrheic dermatitis.",
      "date": "1980s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "FDA Warning",
      "text": "In 2013, the FDA issued a warning regarding the use of oral ketoconazole due to risks of severe liver injury, adrenal gland problems, and harmful drug interactions. The FDA recommended that oral ketoconazole should not be a first-line treatment for any fungal infection.",
      "date": "2013"
