      "text": "Jean Piaget, the Swiss developmental psychologist who originated the theory of cognitive development, was born on August 9, 1896.",
      "date": "1896-08-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Language and Thought of the Child'",
      "text": "In 1923, Jean Piaget published 'The Language and Thought of the Child', which was one of his early works exploring the cognitive development of children.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Judgment and Reasoning in the Child'",
      "text": "In 1924, Piaget published 'Judgment and Reasoning in the Child', further developing his ideas on how children think and reason.",
      "date": "1924"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Child's Conception of the World'",
      "text": "In 1926, Piaget published 'The Child's Conception of the World', where he explored how children perceive and interpret the world around them.",
      "date": "1926"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Child's Conception of Physical Causality'",
      "text": "In 1927, Piaget published 'The Child's Conception of Physical Causality', examining how children understand cause and effect.",
      "date": "1927"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Moral Judgment of the Child'",
      "text": "In 1932, Piaget published 'The Moral Judgment of the Child', which analyzed how children develop moral reasoning.",
      "date": "1932"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Origins of Intelligence in Children'",
      "text": "In 1936, Piaget published 'The Origins of Intelligence in Children', marking a significant contribution to his theory of cognitive development.",
      "date": "1936"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Construction of Reality in the Child'",
      "text": "In 1937, Piaget published 'The Construction of Reality in the Child', further elaborating on how children construct their understanding of the world.",
      "date": "1937"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Psychology of Intelligence'",
      "text": "In 1947, Piaget published 'The Psychology of Intelligence', summarizing his research and theories on cognitive development.",
      "date": "1947"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Child's Conception of Number'",
      "text": "In 1952, Piaget published 'The Child's Conception of Number', which explored how children understand numerical concepts.",
      "date": "1952"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Jean Piaget",
      "text": "Jean Piaget passed away on September 16, 1980, leaving behind a legacy of influential work in developmental psychology.",
      "date": "1980-09-16"
    }
  ]
}

