      "headline": "Birth of Free Software Movement",
      "text": "In 1983, Richard Stallman announced the GNU Project, marking the beginning of the free software movement. The goal was to create a completely free Unix-like operating system.",
      "date": "1983"
    },
    {
      "headline": "GNU General Public License (GPL)",
      "text": "In 1989, the first version of the GNU General Public License (GPL) was released. It was designed to ensure that software licensed under it remains free and open.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
