    {
      "headline": "Open Source Initiative Founded",
      "text": "In 1998, the Open Source Initiative (OSI) was founded to promote and protect open-source software by providing a certification mark and program for open-source licenses.",
      "date": "1998"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mozilla Firefox Released",
      "text": "In 2002, Mozilla Firefox, an open-source web browser, was released. It became one of the most popular web browsers, showcasing the potential of open-source software.",
      "date": "2002"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Git Version Control System",
      "text": "In 2005, Linus Torvalds developed Git, a distributed version control system that became a crucial tool for managing open-source projects.",
      "date": "2005"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Launch of GitHub",
      "text": "In 2008, GitHub was launched as a web-based platform for version control using Git. It became a central hub for open-source collaboration.",
      "date": "2008"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of Android",
      "text": "In 2008, the Android operating system, based on the Linux kernel and other open-source software, was released. It became the world's most popular mobile operating system.",
