      "text": "Maria Theresa died on November 29, 1780, marking the end of her reign and a significant moment for the Habsburg-Lorraine dynasty.",
      "date": "1780-11-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Joseph II becomes Holy Roman Emperor",
      "text": "Joseph II, the eldest son of Maria Theresa and Francis I, became Holy Roman Emperor in 1765, co-ruling with his mother until her death in 1780, and then ruling alone until his death in 1790.",
      "date": "1765"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Leopold II becomes Holy Roman Emperor",
      "text": "Leopold II, the brother of Joseph II, succeeded him as Holy Roman Emperor in 1790, ruling until his death in 1792.",
      "date": "1790"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Francis II becomes Holy Roman Emperor",
      "text": "Francis II, son of Leopold II, became Holy Roman Emperor in 1792. He later dissolved the Holy Roman Empire in 1806 and became Francis I of Austria.",
      "date": "1792"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire",
      "text": "In 1806, Francis II dissolved the Holy Roman Empire following military defeats by Napoleon, marking the end of the empire and the beginning of the Austrian Empire.",
      "date": "1806"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Austrian Empire",
      "text": "In 1804, prior to the dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire, Francis II declared the formation of the Austrian Empire, becoming Francis I of Austria.",
      "date": "1804"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Austro-Hungarian Empire",
      "text": "The Austro-Hungarian Empire, ruled by the Habsburg-Lorraine dynasty, was dissolved in 1918 following World War I.",
      "date": "1918"
    }
  ]
}

