      "headline": "Formation of Sonderkommandos",
      "text": "Sonderkommandos were first formed in 1941 as Nazi Germany began implementing the Final Solution, the plan to exterminate the Jewish population of Europe. These units were composed of Jewish prisoners forced to assist in the disposal of bodies from gas chambers.",
      "date": "1941"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sonderkommando Revolt at Auschwitz",
      "text": "On October 7, 1944, members of the Sonderkommando at Auschwitz-Birkenau staged a revolt. They attacked the SS guards, destroyed Crematorium IV, and attempted to escape. The revolt was ultimately suppressed, and many of the participants were killed.",
      "date": "1944-10-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Liberation of Auschwitz",
      "text": "On January 27, 1945, Auschwitz concentration camp was liberated by Soviet forces. The remaining Sonderkommando members were freed, although many had already been killed or transferred to other camps.",
      "date": "1945-01-27"
    }
  ]
}

