      "text": "On January 30, 1649, King Charles I was executed, marking the end of the monarchy and paving the way for the establishment of the Commonwealth of England.",
      "date": "1649-01-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Declaration of the Commonwealth",
      "text": "On May 19, 1649, the Rump Parliament adopted 'An Act declaring England to be a Commonwealth', officially establishing the Commonwealth of England.",
      "date": "1649-05-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cromwellian Conquest of Ireland",
      "text": "From 1649 to 1653, Oliver Cromwell led a military campaign in Ireland to subdue Irish resistance to the Commonwealth.",
      "date": "1649"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Dunbar",
      "text": "On September 3, 1650, the Battle of Dunbar took place, where Oliver Cromwell's forces defeated the Scottish Covenanters.",
