      "text": "Alexander the Great begins his conquests in 336 BCE, creating one of the largest empires in history by the time of his death in 323 BCE.",
      "date": "-0336"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Hellenistic Period",
      "text": "Following Alexander's death in 323 BCE, the Hellenistic period begins, characterized by the spread of Greek culture across the Mediterranean and Near East.",
      "date": "-0323"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Roman Conquest of Greece",
      "text": "Greece falls under Roman control after the Battle of Corinth in 146 BCE, marking the end of Greek political independence.",
      "date": "-0146"
