      "text": "On January 17, 1961, Patrice Lumumba, the first Prime Minister of the Republic of the Congo, was assassinated after being captured by forces loyal to Katanga.",
      "date": "1961-01-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Stanleyville Government",
      "text": "In August 1961, Antoine Gizenga established a rival government in Stanleyville, claiming to be the legitimate government of the Congo.",
      "date": "1961-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Katanga Secession",
      "text": "On January 15, 1963, the secession of Katanga ended as UN forces took control of the province.",
      "date": "1963-01-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rebellion in Kwilu and Eastern Congo",
      "text": "In 1964, rebellions broke out in Kwilu and Eastern Congo, led by Pierre Mulele and the Simba rebels, respectively.",
      "date": "1964"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Dragon Rouge",
      "text": "On November 24, 1964, Belgian and American forces launched Operation Dragon Rouge to rescue hostages held by Simba rebels in Stanleyville.",
      "date": "1964-11-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mobutu's Second Coup",
      "text": "On November 25, 1965, Joseph-Désiré Mobutu seized power in a coup, marking the end of the Congo Crisis and beginning his long rule.",
      "date": "1965-11-25"
    }
  ]
}

