    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Video on Demand",
      "text": "Video on demand (VOD) systems were first introduced in the early 1990s, allowing users to select and watch video content when they choose to, rather than at a scheduled broadcast time.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First VOD Trials",
      "text": "In 1992, the first VOD trials began in the United Kingdom and the United States, marking the beginning of the technology's development and testing phase.",
      "date": "1992"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Commercial Launch of VOD",
      "text": "The first commercial VOD service was launched in Hong Kong in 1998 by the company iTV, providing a new way for users to access video content.",
      "date": "1998"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion of VOD Services",
      "text": "Throughout the early 2000s, VOD services expanded globally, with cable and satellite television providers offering VOD as part of their service packages.",
      "date": "2000"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rise of Internet-based VOD",
      "text": "In the mid-2000s, internet-based VOD services began to rise, with platforms like YouTube (launched in 2005) allowing users to upload and watch videos online.",
      "date": "2005"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Netflix Launches Streaming Service",
      "text": "In 2007, Netflix launched its streaming service, allowing subscribers to watch a wide variety of TV shows and movies on demand over the internet.",
      "date": "2007"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of OTT Services",
      "text": "The late 2000s and early 2010s saw the introduction of over-the-top (OTT) media services, which deliver content directly to viewers via the internet, bypassing traditional cable or satellite television.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Growth of VOD and OTT Platforms",
      "text": "By the 2010s, VOD and OTT platforms such as Netflix, Hulu, and Amazon Prime Video had become major players in the media industry, significantly impacting traditional television viewing habits.",
      "date": "2010"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Global Expansion of VOD Services",
      "text": "Throughout the 2010s, VOD services expanded globally, with many new regional and international platforms emerging to cater to diverse audiences.",
      "date": "2015"
    },
    {
      "headline": "COVID-19 Pandemic Boosts VOD Usage",
      "text": "During the COVID-19 pandemic in 2020, the usage of VOD services surged as people spent more time at home, accelerating the shift from traditional TV to digital streaming.",
      "date": "2020"
    }
  ]
}

