      "headline": "Cuban Missile Crisis",
      "text": "In October 1962, the Cuban Missile Crisis brought the world to the brink of nuclear war, as the United States and the Soviet Union faced off over Soviet missiles in Cuba.",
      "date": "1962-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty",
      "text": "The Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty (NPT) was signed on July 1, 1968, aiming to prevent the spread of nuclear weapons and promote peaceful uses of nuclear energy.",
      "date": "1968-07-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Strategic Arms Limitation Talks (SALT I)",
      "text": "In 1972, the United States and the Soviet Union signed the SALT I treaty, which limited the number of strategic ballistic missile launchers.",
      "date": "1972"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of the Cold War",
      "text": "The Cold War ended in 1991 with the dissolution of the Soviet Union, reducing the immediate threat of nuclear warfare.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
