      "headline": "Emergence of Techno",
      "text": "Techno music emerged in the mid-1980s in Detroit, Michigan, USA. It was developed by a group of African American artists including Juan Atkins, Derrick May, and Kevin Saunderson, often referred to as the 'Belleville Three'.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'No UFOs' by Model 500",
      "text": "In 1985, Juan Atkins released 'No UFOs' under the alias Model 500. This track is considered one of the first techno records.",
