      "headline": "Establishment of the Imperial Diet",
      "text": "The Imperial Diet was established in 1890 under the Meiji Constitution. It was the first national legislature of Japan, marking a significant step in the country's modernization and adoption of Western-style governance.",
      "date": "1890"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Session of the Imperial Diet",
      "text": "The first session of the Imperial Diet was convened on November 29, 1890. This session marked the beginning of legislative governance in Japan under the Meiji Constitution.",
      "date": "1890-11-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the Post-War Constitution",
      "text": "In 1947, the post-war constitution was adopted, transforming the Imperial Diet into the National Diet. This change marked the establishment of a more democratic and modern legislative system in Japan.",
      "date": "1947"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Session of the National Diet",
      "text": "The first session of the National Diet under the new constitution was held on May 20, 1947. This session marked the beginning of the National Diet's role in Japan's post-war governance.",
      "date": "1947-05-20"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Opening of the National Diet Building",
      "text": "The National Diet Building, located in Nagatachō, Chiyoda, Tokyo, serves as the meeting place for both houses of the Diet. It was completed in 1936 and remains a symbol of Japan's legislative authority.",
      "date": "1936"
    }
  ]
}

