      "headline": "First Lebensborn Home Opens",
      "text": "The first Lebensborn home opened in 1936 in Steinhöring, Bavaria. These homes were designed to provide care and support for unmarried mothers and their children, ensuring they met the Nazi racial criteria.",
      "date": "1936"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion Across Nazi-Occupied Europe",
      "text": "During World War II, Lebensborn expanded its operations across Nazi-occupied Europe, establishing homes in countries such as Norway, France, and Belgium. The program aimed to assimilate children who met Aryan criteria into German society.",
      "date": "1940"
    },
