      "headline": "Cornwallis Code and Permanent Settlement",
      "text": "During his tenure in India, Cornwallis enacted the Cornwallis Code and the Permanent Settlement in 1793, which reformed the administration and land revenue systems.",
      "date": "1793"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lord Lieutenant of Ireland",
      "text": "In 1798, Cornwallis was appointed as the Lord Lieutenant of Ireland, where he played a key role in the passage of the Act of Union in 1800.",
      "date": "1798"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Charles Cornwallis",
      "text": "Charles Cornwallis died on October 5, 1805, in Ghazipur, India, while serving a second term as Governor-General of India.",
      "date": "1805-10-05"
    }
  ]
}

