      "headline": "Ancient History of Guwahati",
      "text": "Guwahati's history dates back to ancient times, with references in the Mahabharata and other ancient texts. It was known as Pragjyotishpura, the capital of the ancient kingdom of Kamarupa.",
      "date": "-0500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Kamakhya Temple",
      "text": "The Kamakhya Temple, one of the most important Hindu temples dedicated to the mother goddess Kamakhya, was established in the early centuries CE. It is a significant pilgrimage site.",
      "date": "0600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Medieval Period",
      "text": "During the medieval period, Guwahati was an important city under the rule of the Ahom kingdom, which ruled Assam for nearly 600 years.",
      "date": "1200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Saraighat",
      "text": "In 1671, the Battle of Saraighat took place near Guwahati, where the Ahom forces led by Lachit Borphukan defeated the Mughal army, marking a significant event in the city's history.",
      "date": "1671"
    },
    {
      "headline": "British Colonial Period",
      "text": "During the British colonial period, Guwahati became an important administrative and commercial center in Assam.",
      "date": "1826"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Post-Independence Development",
      "text": "After India's independence in 1947, Guwahati experienced rapid development and urbanization, becoming the largest city in Assam and the gateway to Northeast India.",
      "date": "1947"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Dispur as Capital",
      "text": "In 1973, Dispur, a locality within Guwahati, was made the capital of Assam, further increasing the city's political significance.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Modern Growth and Development",
      "text": "In the 21st century, Guwahati has grown rapidly, becoming one of the fastest-growing cities in India, with significant improvements in infrastructure and connectivity.",
      "date": "2000"
    }
  ]
}

{
