      "text": "M. S. Swaminathan was born on August 7, 1925, in Kumbakonam, Tamil Nadu, India.",
      "date": "1925-08-07"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Graduation in Agricultural Science",
      "text": "In 1944, Swaminathan graduated with a Bachelor of Science degree in Agricultural Science from the University of Madras.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Postgraduate Studies",
      "text": "Swaminathan completed his postgraduate studies in genetics and plant breeding at the Indian Agricultural Research Institute (IARI) in New Delhi in 1949.",
      "date": "1949"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Doctorate from University of Cambridge",
      "text": "In 1952, Swaminathan received his Ph.D. in genetics from the University of Cambridge, UK.",
      "date": "1952"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Research at the University of Wisconsin",
      "text": "Swaminathan conducted postdoctoral research at the University of Wisconsin, USA, from 1954 to 1955.",
      "date": "1954"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Joining the Central Rice Research Institute",
      "text": "In 1954, Swaminathan joined the Central Rice Research Institute in Cuttack, India, where he began his work on high-yielding varieties of rice.",
      "date": "1954"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Director of the Indian Agricultural Research Institute",
      "text": "Swaminathan became the Director of the Indian Agricultural Research Institute in 1966, where he played a crucial role in the Green Revolution in India.",
      "date": "1966"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of High-Yielding Varieties",
      "text": "During the late 1960s, Swaminathan introduced and developed high-yielding varieties of wheat and rice, significantly increasing food production in India.",
      "date": "1960s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Chairman of the National Commission on Agriculture",
      "text": "In 1972, Swaminathan was appointed as the Chairman of the National Commission on Agriculture in India.",
      "date": "1972"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First World Food Prize Laureate",
      "text": "In 1987, Swaminathan became the first recipient of the World Food Prize for his contributions to the Green Revolution.",
      "date": "1987"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the M. S. Swaminathan Research Foundation",
      "text": "In 1988, Swaminathan founded the M. S. Swaminathan Research Foundation in Chennai, focusing on sustainable agriculture and rural development.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of M. S. Swaminathan",
      "text": "M. S. Swaminathan passed away on September 28, 2023, in Chennai, Tamil Nadu, India.",
      "date": "2023-09-28"
    }
  ]
}

