      "text": "In 1881, Simon Newcomb, a Canadian-American astronomer and mathematician, observed that the earlier pages of logarithm books were much more worn than the later pages. He published a paper in the American Journal of Mathematics describing this phenomenon, which later became known as Newcomb's law.",
      "date": "1881"
    },
