      "text": "The Malleus Maleficarum, written by Heinrich Kramer, was first published in the German city of Speyer in 1487. It became the most famous treatise on witchcraft and was used to support witch hunts.",
      "date": "1487"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Impact on Witch Hunts",
      "text": "The Malleus Maleficarum significantly influenced the witch hunts of the 15th and 16th centuries. It was used as a guide by inquisitors and secular courts to identify, prosecute, and execute alleged witches.",
      "date": "1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Condemnation by the Catholic Church",
      "text": "Despite its initial influence, the Malleus Maleficarum was later condemned by the Catholic Church. The Church distanced itself from the book's extreme views and methods.",
