      "headline": "Introduction of NFC Technology",
      "text": "Near-field communication (NFC) technology was introduced as a set of communication protocols that enables communication between two electronic devices over a short distance of 4 cm or less. It is based on inductive coupling between two electromagnetic coils present on NFC-enabled devices.",
      "date": "2002"
    },
    {
      "headline": "NFC Forum Founded",
      "text": "The NFC Forum was founded to advance the use of NFC technology by developing specifications, ensuring interoperability among devices and services, and educating the market about NFC technology. The founding members included Nokia, Philips, and Sony.",
      "date": "2004"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First NFC-enabled Phone Released",
      "text": "The first NFC-enabled phone, the Nokia 6131, was released, marking a significant milestone in the adoption of NFC technology in consumer electronics.",
      "date": "2006"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Google Wallet Launch",
      "text": "Google launched Google Wallet, a mobile payment system that uses NFC technology to allow users to make payments by tapping their phones at point-of-sale terminals.",
      "date": "2011"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Apple Pay Introduction",
      "text": "Apple introduced Apple Pay, a mobile payment and digital wallet service that uses NFC technology to enable contactless payments on iPhones and other Apple devices.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
    {
      "headline": "NFC in Public Transport",
      "text": "NFC technology began to be widely adopted in public transportation systems around the world, allowing users to pay for fares by tapping their NFC-enabled devices.",
      "date": "2015"
    },
    {
      "headline": "NFC in Contactless Payments",
      "text": "NFC technology became a standard feature in smartphones, facilitating the widespread adoption of contactless payments globally.",
      "date": "2016"
    }
  ]
}

