      "headline": "First Assembly Session",
      "text": "The first session of the Rajasthan Legislative Assembly was held in 1952, marking the beginning of legislative governance in the state.",
      "date": "1952"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of Bicameral Legislature",
      "text": "In 1956, Rajasthan had a bicameral legislature with the establishment of the Rajasthan Legislative Council, which functioned alongside the Legislative Assembly.",
      "date": "1956"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abolition of Legislative Council",
      "text": "The Rajasthan Legislative Council was abolished in 1974, making the Rajasthan Legislative Assembly a unicameral body.",
      "date": "1974"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Increase in Assembly Seats",
      "text": "The number of seats in the Rajasthan Legislative Assembly was increased to 200 in 1977 to accommodate the growing population and ensure better representation.",
