      "headline": "Formation of the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies",
      "text": "The International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC) was founded on May 5, 1919, in Paris, France, to coordinate international relief efforts and promote humanitarian principles.",
      "date": "1919-05-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the Red Crescent Emblem",
      "text": "The Red Crescent emblem was officially adopted in 1929, recognizing the symbol used by several Muslim countries as an alternative to the Red Cross.",
      "date": "1929"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Nobel Peace Prize Awarded to the ICRC",
      "text": "The International Committee of the Red Cross was awarded the Nobel Peace Prize in 1944 for its humanitarian efforts during World War II.",
      "date": "1944"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the Red Crystal Emblem",
      "text": "In 2005, the Red Crystal was adopted as an additional emblem to provide a neutral symbol for use in situations where the Red Cross or Red Crescent might not be appropriate.",
