      "headline": "Establishment of the First Law Commission",
      "text": "The first Law Commission of India was established in 1834 under the Charter Act of 1833. It was chaired by Thomas Babington Macaulay.",
      "date": "1834"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Drafting of the Indian Penal Code",
      "text": "The Indian Penal Code was drafted on the recommendations of the first Law Commission under the chairmanship of Thomas Babington Macaulay.",
      "date": "1837"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Enactment of the Indian Penal Code",
      "text": "The Indian Penal Code was enacted and came into force in the subcontinent during British rule in 1862.",
      "date": "1862"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Non-application in Princely States",
      "text": "The Indian Penal Code did not apply automatically in the Princely states, which had their own courts and legal systems until the 1940s.",
      "date": "1940"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Independence of India",
      "text": "India gained independence from British rule in 1947, and the Indian Penal Code was inherited as the official criminal code.",
      "date": "1947"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Repeal and Replacement by Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita",
      "text": "The Indian Penal Code was repealed and replaced by the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) in December 2023.",
      "date": "2023-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita Comes into Effect",
      "text": "The Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) came into effect on 1 July 2024, replacing the Indian Penal Code.",
