      "headline": "Slavery in Ancient Rome",
      "text": "In ancient Rome, slavery was a common practice and included people from various European ethnic groups. Slavery was often based on socio-economic status and national affiliation.",
      "date": "-0753"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arab Slave Trade",
      "text": "Beginning in the 7th century, the Arab slave trade involved the capture and sale of European slaves, particularly women, who were sought after as concubines in the Muslim world.",
      "date": "0700"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Barbary Slave Trade",
      "text": "From the 16th to the 19th century, the Barbary pirates from North Africa captured Europeans and sold them into slavery. This trade was particularly active along the Mediterranean coast.",
      "date": "1500"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ottoman Slave Trade",
      "text": "During the Ottoman Empire, which lasted from 1299 to 1922, Europeans were among those enslaved. The empire's expansion into Europe led to the capture and enslavement of many Europeans.",
      "date": "1299"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Black Sea Slave Trade",
      "text": "The Black Sea slave trade, active from the 13th to the 18th century, involved the capture and sale of Slavic peoples to the Ottoman Empire and other regions.",
      "date": "1200"
    }
  ]
}

