      "headline": "Scheduled Flight",
      "text": "China Eastern Airlines Flight 5735 was a scheduled domestic passenger flight from Changshui International Airport, Kunming, to Baiyun International Airport, Guangzhou in China.",
      "date": "2022-03-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Crash Incident",
      "text": "At 14:23 CST on 21 March 2022, the Boeing 737-89P aircraft descended steeply mid-flight and struck the ground at high speed in Teng County, Wuzhou, Guangxi, killing all 132 passengers and crew on board.",
      "date": "2022-03-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Investigation",
      "text": "Multiple reports suggest that the airplane was deliberately crashed, but the official investigation by the Civil Aviation Administration of China (CAAC) is ongoing.",
      "date": "2022-03-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Significance of the Crash",
      "text": "It is the third deadliest air crash in China after China Southern Airlines Flight 3943 in 1992 and China Northwest Airlines Flight 2303 in 1994, the deadliest air accident in China Eastern Airlines' history, and the deadliest plane crash in 2022.",
      "date": "2022-03-21"
    }
  ]
}

