      "headline": "Plan Dalet",
      "text": "In March 1948, the Jewish leadership adopted Plan Dalet, a military strategy aimed at securing the territory allotted to the Jewish state and defending Jewish communities.",
      "date": "1948-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Deir Yassin Massacre",
      "text": "On 9 April 1948, Jewish paramilitary groups Irgun and Lehi attacked the Arab village of Deir Yassin, resulting in the massacre of over 100 villagers, which intensified the conflict and led to widespread Arab fear and flight.",
      "date": "1948-04-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Operation Nachshon",
      "text": "From 5 to 20 April 1948, Jewish forces launched Operation Nachshon to break the siege of Jerusalem and secure the road to the city, marking the first large-scale operation by the Haganah.",
      "date": "1948-04-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of British Mandate",
      "text": "On 14 May 1948, the British Mandate officially ended, and the State of Israel was declared. This marked the transition from civil war to the 1948 Arab-Israeli War.",
      "date": "1948-05-14"
    }
  ]
}

