      "headline": "First Flight of the Wright Flyer",
      "text": "On December 17, 1903, the Wright Flyer made the first sustained flight by a manned heavier-than-air powered and controlled aircraft. Orville Wright piloted the aircraft for 12 seconds, covering 120 feet.",
      "date": "1903-12-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Subsequent Flights on First Day",
      "text": "On December 17, 1903, after the first flight, the Wright Flyer made three more flights. The longest flight, piloted by Wilbur Wright, lasted 59 seconds and covered 852 feet.",
      "date": "1903-12-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wright Flyer Damaged",
      "text": "On December 17, 1903, after the fourth flight, a gust of wind overturned the Wright Flyer, severely damaging it. The aircraft was never flown again.",
      "date": "1903-12-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wright Flyer Displayed at the Smithsonian",
      "text": "In 1948, the Wright Flyer was restored and placed on display at the Smithsonian Institution in Washington, D.C., where it remains a centerpiece exhibit.",
      "date": "1948"
    }
  ]
}

