      "headline": "Fortification by Sultan Quli Qutb-ul-Mulk",
      "text": "Following the death of Sultan Mahmood Shah, the Bahmani Sultanate disintegrated and Sultan Quli Qutb-ul-Mulk, who had been appointed as the Governor of Hyderabad by the Bahmani Kings, fortified the city and made it the capital of the Golconda Sultanate.",
      "date": "1518"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Golconda as a Trade Centre",
      "text": "Due to the vicinity of diamond mines, especially the Kollur Mine, Golconda flourished as a trade centre of large diamonds known as Golconda Diamonds.",
      "date": "1600"
    },
    {
      "headline": "UNESCO Tentative List",
      "text": "In 2014, Golconda Fort was put by UNESCO on its 'tentative list' to become a World Heritage Site, along with other forts in the region, under the name Monuments and Forts of the Deccan Sultanate.",
      "date": "2014"
    }
  ]
}

