      "text": "The Battle of Verdun began on February 21, 1916, and continued until December 18, 1916, becoming one of the longest and costliest battles in World War I.",
      "date": "1916-02-21"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of the Somme",
      "text": "The Battle of the Somme began on July 1, 1916, and ended on November 18, 1916, with over one million casualties.",
      "date": "1916-07-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "United States Enters the War",
      "text": "On April 6, 1917, the United States declared war on Germany, joining the Allies in World War I.",
      "date": "1917-04-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russian Revolution",
      "text": "In 1917, the Russian Revolution led to Russia's withdrawal from World War I and the signing of the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk with Germany on March 3, 1918.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Armistice of Compiègne",
      "text": "On November 11, 1918, the Armistice of Compiègne was signed, ending the fighting on the Western Front and effectively concluding World War I.",
      "date": "1918-11-11"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Versailles",
      "text": "The Treaty of Versailles was signed on June 28, 1919, officially ending World War I and imposing heavy reparations and territorial losses on Germany.",
      "date": "1919-06-28"
    }
  ]
}

