      "text": "The Islamic State of Iraq (ISI) was formed in October 2006, following the merger of several insurgent groups in Iraq, including al-Qaeda in Iraq.",
      "date": "2006-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion into Syria",
      "text": "In April 2013, the group expanded into Syria and rebranded itself as the Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant (ISIL), also known as ISIS.",
      "date": "2013-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Declaration of Caliphate",
      "text": "On June 29, 2014, ISIL declared a worldwide caliphate, with Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi as its caliph, and renamed itself the Islamic State (IS).",
      "date": "2014-06-29"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capture of Mosul",
      "text": "In June 2014, ISIL captured Mosul, Iraq's second-largest city, marking a significant territorial gain for the group.",
      "date": "2014-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Kobani",
      "text": "From September 2014 to January 2015, ISIL engaged in a prolonged battle for the Syrian town of Kobani, which ended in ISIL's defeat.",
      "date": "2014-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Tikrit",
      "text": "In March 2015, ISIL lost control of the Iraqi city of Tikrit to Iraqi government forces and allied militias.",
      "date": "2015-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Ramadi",
      "text": "In December 2015, ISIL lost the city of Ramadi to Iraqi government forces, marking another significant territorial loss.",
      "date": "2015-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Fallujah",
      "text": "In June 2016, ISIL lost control of Fallujah, one of its major strongholds in Iraq, to Iraqi government forces.",
      "date": "2016-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Mosul",
      "text": "The battle to retake Mosul from ISIL began in October 2016 and concluded in July 2017 with the city's liberation by Iraqi forces.",
      "date": "2016-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Loss of Raqqa",
      "text": "In October 2017, ISIL lost its de facto capital, Raqqa, to the Syrian Democratic Forces (SDF) backed by the US-led coalition.",
      "date": "2017-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Defeat in Baghouz",
      "text": "In March 2019, ISIL was defeated in its last stronghold in Baghouz, Syria, marking the territorial end of the caliphate.",
      "date": "2019-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi",
