      "headline": "Birth of Adi Shankara",
      "text": "Adi Shankara, the founder of the Shankaracharya tradition, was born in Kaladi, a village in present-day Kerala, India. His birth is traditionally dated to 788 CE.",
      "date": "0788"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of Brahmasutra Bhashya",
      "text": "Adi Shankara completed his commentary on the Brahmasutras, known as the Brahmasutra Bhashya, which is considered one of his most important works. This event is traditionally dated to around 800 CE.",
      "date": "0800"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Mathas",
      "text": "Adi Shankara established four mathas (monasteries) in different regions of India to propagate the Advaita Vedanta philosophy. These mathas are located in Sringeri, Dwaraka, Puri, and Jyotirmath. This event is traditionally dated to around 820 CE.",
      "date": "0820"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Debate with Mandana Mishra",
      "text": "Adi Shankara engaged in a famous debate with the philosopher Mandana Mishra, which is said to have lasted several days. Shankara emerged victorious, and Mandana Mishra became one of his disciples. This event is traditionally dated to around 820 CE.",
      "date": "0820"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Adi Shankara",
      "text": "Adi Shankara is believed to have died at the age of 32 in Kedarnath, in present-day Uttarakhand, India. His death is traditionally dated to 820 CE.",
      "date": "0820"
    }
  ]
}

