      "text": "Ibn Khaldun was born on May 27, 1332, in Tunis, which is in present-day Tunisia.",
      "date": "1332-05-27"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of Education",
      "text": "By 1347, Ibn Khaldun had completed his education, which included studies in the Quran, Arabic linguistics, hadith, sharia (law), and other subjects.",
      "date": "1347"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Political Appointment",
      "text": "In 1352, Ibn Khaldun received his first political appointment as a seal-bearer to the Sultan of Tunis.",
      "date": "1352"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Move to Fez",
      "text": "In 1354, Ibn Khaldun moved to Fez, Morocco, where he joined the court of the Marinid Sultan.",
      "date": "1354"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Imprisonment",
      "text": "In 1357, Ibn Khaldun was imprisoned due to political intrigue and rivalry at the court of Fez.",
      "date": "1357"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release from Prison",
      "text": "Ibn Khaldun was released from prison in 1358 and resumed his political career.",
      "date": "1358"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service in Granada",
      "text": "In 1362, Ibn Khaldun traveled to Granada, where he served as an ambassador for the Sultan of Granada to the court of Pedro the Cruel of Castile.",
      "date": "1362"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Return to North Africa",
      "text": "In 1375, Ibn Khaldun returned to North Africa, where he sought refuge in a fortress in Algeria to focus on his writing.",
      "date": "1375"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Muqaddimah",
      "text": "In 1377, Ibn Khaldun completed his seminal work, the Muqaddimah, which is considered a pioneering work in the fields of sociology, historiography, and economics.",
      "date": "1377"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appointment in Cairo",
      "text": "In 1382, Ibn Khaldun moved to Cairo, where he was appointed as a professor of Maliki law at the Al-Azhar University.",
      "date": "1382"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Meeting with Timur",
      "text": "In 1401, Ibn Khaldun met with the conqueror Timur (Tamerlane) outside the city of Damascus, where he was held for several months.",
      "date": "1401"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Ibn Khaldun",
      "text": "Ibn Khaldun died on March 17, 1406, in Cairo, Egypt.",
      "date": "1406-03-17"
    }
  ]
}

