      "headline": "Libertarian Party's Growth",
      "text": "In the 1990s, the Libertarian Party continued to grow, fielding candidates in various local, state, and national elections, and advocating for policies based on individual liberty and limited government.",
      "date": "1990"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ron Paul's Return to Congress",
      "text": "Ron Paul returned to Congress in 1997, serving as a Republican with strong libertarian principles, and became known for his advocacy of non-interventionist foreign policy and fiscal conservatism.",
      "date": "1997"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ron Paul's 2008 Presidential Campaign",
      "text": "Ron Paul ran for President again in 2008 as a Republican, gaining a large following and bringing libertarian ideas to a broader audience.",
