      "text": "In 1664, the English seized New Amsterdam from the Dutch, renaming it New York. This marked the end of Dutch control over the colony.",
      "date": "1664"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Treaty of Breda",
      "text": "The Treaty of Breda was signed in 1667, ending the Second Anglo-Dutch War. The Dutch retained control of Suriname while ceding New Netherland to the English.",
      "date": "1667"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dutch Capture of Banda Islands",
      "text": "The Dutch East India Company took control of the Banda Islands in 1621, securing a monopoly over the lucrative nutmeg trade.",
