      "text": "In 1574, a fire damaged parts of the palace, leading to reconstruction efforts under Sultan Selim II, which included the rebuilding of the kitchens and other sections.",
      "date": "1574"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Palace as Primary Residence",
      "text": "In 1856, Sultan Abdülmecid I moved the court to the newly built Dolmabahçe Palace, marking the end of Topkapı Palace as the primary residence of the Ottoman sultans.",
      "date": "1856"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Conversion to a Museum",
      "text": "Following the establishment of the Republic of Turkey, Topkapı Palace was transformed into a museum in 1924, opening its doors to the public.",
      "date": "1924"
