      "headline": "I-95 Fully Connected in the Northeast",
      "text": "By 1976, I-95 was fully connected in the northeastern United States, providing a continuous route from Maine to Virginia.",
      "date": "1976"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Woodrow Wilson Bridge",
      "text": "The Woodrow Wilson Bridge, which carries I-95 over the Potomac River between Maryland and Virginia, was completed in 1961. However, it was replaced with a new bridge in 2008 to accommodate increased traffic.",
