      "headline": "Life Peerages Act 1958",
      "text": "The Life Peerages Act 1958 was enacted, allowing for the creation of life peers with the rank of baron. These peers are appointed by the monarch on the advice of the prime minister and are entitled to sit and vote in the House of Lords.",
      "date": "1958"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Appellate Jurisdiction Act 1876",
      "text": "Prior to the Life Peerages Act 1958, life peers of baronial rank could be created under the Appellate Jurisdiction Act 1876 specifically for senior judges.",
      "date": "1876"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Life Peerages since 2009",
      "text": "Since 2009, all life peerages conferred have been created under the Life Peerages Act 1958 with the rank of baron, except for the Dukedom of Edinburgh awarded for life to Prince Edward in 2023.",
      "date": "2009"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dukedom of Edinburgh awarded to Prince Edward",
