      "text": "The first recognized land speed record was set by Gaston de Chasseloup-Laubat in an electric car on December 18, 1898, reaching a speed of 63.15 km/h (39.24 mph).",
      "date": "1898-12-18"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Internal Combustion Engine Record",
      "text": "Camille Jenatzy set a new land speed record on January 17, 1899, in a vehicle powered by an internal combustion engine, reaching 66.66 km/h (41.42 mph).",
