      "text": "Ajax was instrumental in defending the Greek ships from being burned by the Trojans, showcasing his bravery and strength.",
      "date": "-1189"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Achilles",
      "text": "After the death of Achilles, Ajax competed with Odysseus for the armor of Achilles. This event is a significant part of the Trojan War narrative.",
      "date": "-1184"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Ajax the Great",
      "text": "Following the decision to award Achilles' armor to Odysseus, Ajax fell into a deep rage and eventually took his own life. His death is a tragic part of the Trojan War saga.",
      "date": "-1184"
    }
  ]
}

