      "headline": "Murray Rothbard's Influence",
      "text": "In the mid-20th century, Murray Rothbard, an economist and political theorist, became a leading figure in the development of anarcho-capitalism. He combined elements of classical liberalism and Austrian economics to form the basis of the philosophy.",
      "date": "1950"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Man, Economy, and State'",
      "text": "In 1962, Murray Rothbard published 'Man, Economy, and State', a comprehensive work that laid out his economic theories and the foundations of anarcho-capitalism.",
