    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of the Term 'Anarcho-Capitalism'",
      "text": "The term 'anarcho-capitalism' was popularized by Murray Rothbard in the 1960s to describe his vision of a stateless society based on voluntary transactions and private property.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'For a New Liberty'",
      "text": "In 1973, Rothbard published 'For a New Liberty: The Libertarian Manifesto', which further elaborated on anarcho-capitalist principles and advocated for a society without government.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Foundation of the Ludwig von Mises Institute",
      "text": "In 1982, the Ludwig von Mises Institute was founded, promoting Austrian economics and libertarian political theory, including anarcho-capitalism.",
      "date": "1982"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Machinery of Freedom'",
      "text": "David D. Friedman published 'The Machinery of Freedom' in 1973, offering a utilitarian approach to anarcho-capitalism and exploring how a stateless society might function.",
      "date": "1973"
    },
