      "headline": "Founding of United Artists",
      "text": "United Artists was founded on February 5, 1919, by Charlie Chaplin, D.W. Griffith, Mary Pickford, and Douglas Fairbanks. The company was established to allow actors to control their own financial and artistic interests rather than being dependent upon commercial studios.",
      "date": "1919-02-05"
