    {
      "headline": "Great Flood of 1913",
      "text": "In March 1913, Dayton experienced a devastating flood that resulted in widespread destruction and loss of life. This event led to the creation of the Miami Conservancy District to prevent future floods.",
      "date": "1913-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Wright Brothers' First Flight",
      "text": "Orville and Wilbur Wright, who were from Dayton, achieved the first powered flight on December 17, 1903, in Kitty Hawk, North Carolina. Their work in Dayton was crucial to this achievement.",
