      "text": "In 1876, Baden-Powell was commissioned as a lieutenant in the 13th Hussars of the British Army.",
      "date": "1876"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publishes 'Reconnaissance and Scouting'",
      "text": "In 1884, Baden-Powell published his first book, 'Reconnaissance and Scouting', which was based on his military experiences.",
      "date": "1884"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publishes 'Aids to Scouting'",
      "text": "In 1899, Baden-Powell published 'Aids to Scouting for N.-C.Os and Men', a military training manual that later influenced the Scouting movement.",
      "date": "1899"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Siege of Mafeking",
      "text": "From 1899 to 1900, Baden-Powell successfully defended the town of Mafeking during the Second Boer War, becoming a national hero in Britain.",
      "date": "1899"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publishes 'Scouting for Boys'",
      "text": "In 1908, Baden-Powell published 'Scouting for Boys', a handbook that became the foundation of the Boy Scouts movement.",
      "date": "1908"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of The Boy Scouts Association",
      "text": "In 1908, following the success of 'Scouting for Boys', Baden-Powell founded The Boy Scouts Association.",
      "date": "1908"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Founding of The Girl Guides Association",
      "text": "In 1910, Baden-Powell, along with his sister Agnes, founded The Girl Guides Association.",
      "date": "1910"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Marriage to Olave St Clair Soames",
      "text": "On October 30, 1912, Baden-Powell married Olave St Clair Soames.",
      "date": "1912-10-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Retirement from the Army",
      "text": "In 1910, Baden-Powell retired from the British Army to focus on the Scouting movement.",
      "date": "1910"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Created 1st Baron Baden-Powell",
      "text": "In 1929, Baden-Powell was created 1st Baron Baden-Powell of Gilwell, in recognition of his services to the Scouting movement.",
      "date": "1929"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Robert Baden-Powell",
      "text": "Robert Baden-Powell died on January 8, 1941, in Nyeri, Kenya.",
