      "headline": "Discovery of Schistosomiasis",
      "text": "The disease schistosomiasis was first described in 1851 by Theodor Bilharz, a German physician working in Egypt. He discovered the parasitic flatworms, later named schistosomes, that cause the disease.",
      "date": "1851"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Identification of Schistosoma haematobium",
      "text": "In 1852, Theodor Bilharz identified Schistosoma haematobium as the causative agent of urinary schistosomiasis.",
      "date": "1852"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Identification of Schistosoma mansoni",
      "text": "In 1907, Louis Westenra Sambon identified Schistosoma mansoni, another species of schistosome responsible for intestinal schistosomiasis.",
      "date": "1907"
