      "text": "According to tradition, Thomas the Apostle arrived in India in 52 AD to spread Christianity. He is believed to have landed at Muziris (modern-day Kodungallur in Kerala).",
      "date": "0052"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Christian Communities",
      "text": "Thomas the Apostle is credited with establishing seven and a half churches in Kerala, laying the foundation for the Saint Thomas Christian community.",
