      "headline": "Death of Dashrath Manjhi's Wife",
      "text": "In 1959, Dashrath Manjhi's wife died after being injured from falling from a mountain. The mountain blocked easy access to a nearby hospital, preventing timely medical care.",
      "date": "1959"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Start of Mountain Carving",
      "text": "Motivated by his wife's death, Dashrath Manjhi began carving a path through a ridge of hills using only a hammer and a chisel in 1960.",
      "date": "1960"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of the Path",
      "text": "After 22 years of work, Dashrath Manjhi completed the 110-metre-long, 9.1-metre-wide, and 7.7-metre-deep path in 1982, reducing the travel distance between Atri and Wazirganj blocks of Gaya district from 55 km to 15 km.",
      "date": "1982"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Recognition by Chief Minister",
      "text": "Dashrath Manjhi travelled to New Delhi to seek recognition for his work and was rewarded by the then Chief Minister of Bihar, Nitish Kumar.",
      "date": "Date not specified"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Dashrath Manjhi",
      "text": "Dashrath Manjhi passed away on August 17, 2007, after battling gallbladder cancer.",
      "date": "2007-08-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Postage Stamp Issued",
      "text": "In 2016, the Indian Post issued a postage stamp featuring Dashrath Manjhi, honoring his remarkable achievement.",
      "date": "2016"
    }
  ]
}

