      "headline": "Recognition and Analysis",
      "text": "Sealioning began to be recognized and analyzed as a form of online harassment and trolling. It is characterized by incessant, bad-faith invitations to engage in debate, often likened to a denial-of-service attack targeted at human beings.",
      "date": "2014"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cultural Impact",
      "text": "The term gained popularity and was widely used to describe certain behaviors on social media platforms, particularly Twitter. The Independent referred to the Wondermark comic as 'the most apt description of Twitter you'll ever see'.",
