      "date": "-0380"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Phaedo",
      "text": "In 'Phaedo', written around 360 BCE, Plato discusses the immortality of the soul and the Theory of Forms, suggesting that true knowledge is the understanding of these Forms.",
      "date": "-0360"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Phaedrus",
      "text": "In 'Phaedrus', also written around 360 BCE, Plato explores the concept of Forms in the context of love and beauty, emphasizing their eternal and perfect nature.",
      "date": "-0360"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Influence on Western Philosophy",
      "text": "The Theory of Forms has had a profound influence on Western philosophy, shaping metaphysical thought and influencing philosophers such as Aristotle, who critiqued and developed his own ideas in response to Plato's theory.",
      "date": "-0347"
    }
  ]
}

