      "text": "In 1910, Rilke published his only novel, 'The Notebooks of Malte Laurids Brigge' ('Die Aufzeichnungen des Malte Laurids Brigge'), which is considered a seminal work of modernist literature.",
      "date": "1910"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Writing of 'Duino Elegies'",
      "text": "Rilke began writing the 'Duino Elegies' in 1912 while staying at Duino Castle near Trieste. This work would become one of his most acclaimed collections of poetry.",
      "date": "1912"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Completion of 'Duino Elegies'",
      "text": "Rilke completed the 'Duino Elegies' in February 1922, after a decade of intermittent work on the collection.",
      "date": "1922-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Sonnets to Orpheus'",
      "text": "In 1923, Rilke published 'Sonnets to Orpheus' ('Die Sonette an Orpheus'), a collection of 55 sonnets written in a burst of creativity in February 1922.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Rainer Maria Rilke",
      "text": "Rainer Maria Rilke died on December 29, 1926, at the age of 51, in the Valmont Sanatorium in Switzerland, due to leukemia.",
      "date": "1926-12-29"
    }
  ]
}

{
