      "text": "The College of Sorbonne, a theological college, was founded by Robert de Sorbon and chartered by King Louis IX around 1257. It became a significant part of the University of Paris.",
      "date": "1257"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Closure during the French Revolution",
      "text": "The University of Paris was closed from 1793 to 1806 during the French Revolution, reflecting the period's political and social upheaval.",
      "date": "1793"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Reopening after the French Revolution",
      "text": "The University of Paris reopened in 1806 after being closed during the French Revolution, resuming its role as a major educational institution.",
      "date": "1806"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Dissolution and Reorganization",
      "text": "In 1970, the University of Paris was dissolved and reorganized into 13 autonomous universities, marking the end of its existence as a single entity.",
