      "headline": "Invention of Flash Memory",
      "text": "Flash memory was invented by Fujio Masuoka while working for Toshiba in 1980. It was named 'flash' because the erasure process reminded Masuoka of a camera flash.",
      "date": "1980"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of NOR Flash",
      "text": "NOR flash was introduced by Intel in 1988. It was the first type of flash memory to be commercially available and is known for its fast read speeds.",
      "date": "1988"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of NAND Flash",
      "text": "NAND flash was introduced by Toshiba in 1989. It is known for its high storage capacity and is widely used in USB drives, memory cards, and solid-state drives.",
      "date": "1989"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Commercial NAND Flash Product",
      "text": "The first commercial NAND flash product was introduced by SanDisk in 1991. It marked the beginning of NAND flash's widespread use in consumer electronics.",
      "date": "1991"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Development of Multi-Level Cell (MLC) Technology",
      "text": "In the mid-1990s, Multi-Level Cell (MLC) technology was developed, allowing flash memory cells to store more than one bit per cell, increasing storage capacity.",
      "date": "1990s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Introduction of 3D NAND",
      "text": "3D NAND technology was introduced in 2013 by Samsung. It involves stacking memory cells vertically to increase density and storage capacity.",
      "date": "2013"
    }
  ]
}

