      "headline": "Development of Novichok Agents Begins",
      "text": "The development of Novichok agents began in the Soviet Union at the GosNIIOKhT state chemical research institute. This development took place between 1971 and 1993.",
      "date": "1971"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Novichok Development",
      "text": "The development of Novichok agents concluded in 1993. These agents were part of a secret Soviet program to create more potent chemical weapons.",
      "date": "1993"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Public Disclosure of Novichok",
      "text": "In the 1990s, information about Novichok agents became public through the disclosures of Vil Mirzayanov, a Russian chemist who worked on the program. He revealed the existence of these agents and their potential dangers.",
      "date": "1990s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Salisbury Poisoning Incident",
      "text": "On March 4, 2018, former Russian spy Sergei Skripal and his daughter Yulia were poisoned with a Novichok agent in Salisbury, England. This incident brought international attention to the use of Novichok as a chemical weapon.",
      "date": "2018-03-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Amesbury Poisoning Incident",
      "text": "On June 30, 2018, two British nationals, Charlie Rowley and Dawn Sturgess, were exposed to a Novichok agent in Amesbury, England. Dawn Sturgess later died as a result of the poisoning.",
