      "headline": "Introduction of Pankration to the Olympic Games",
      "text": "Pankration was introduced into the Greek Olympic Games in 648 BC. It was an unarmed combat sport that combined techniques from boxing and wrestling, along with kicking, holds, joint locks, and chokes, making it similar to modern mixed martial arts.",
      "date": "-0648"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Popularity in Ancient Greece",
