    },
    {
      "headline": "Inclusion in Other Panhellenic Games",
      "text": "Following its introduction to the Olympic Games, pankration was also included in other major Greek athletic festivals, such as the Isthmian, Nemean, and Pythian Games.",
      "date": "-0648"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cultural Significance",
      "text": "Pankration was not only a sport but also a part of Greek culture and mythology. It was believed to have been used by heroes such as Heracles and Theseus.",
      "date": "-0648"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Decline of Pankration",
      "text": "With the rise of the Roman Empire and the eventual decline of the ancient Greek civilization, pankration's popularity waned, and it eventually disappeared as a formal competitive sport.",
