      "headline": "Establishment of Sikorsky Aircraft",
      "text": "Sikorsky Aircraft was established by Russian aviation pioneer Igor Sikorsky in 1923. The company was founded in Stratford, Connecticut, and became one of the first to manufacture helicopters for both civilian and military use.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Successful Helicopter Flight",
      "text": "In 1939, Sikorsky Aircraft achieved its first successful helicopter flight with the VS-300, which was designed by Igor Sikorsky. This marked a significant milestone in the development of rotary-wing aircraft.",
