      "headline": "Tuskegee Syphilis Study Begins",
      "text": "In 1932, the Tuskegee Syphilis Study began. This study was conducted by the U.S. Public Health Service and involved 600 African American men, 399 with syphilis and 201 without. The study aimed to observe the natural progression of untreated syphilis.",
      "date": "1932"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Guatemala Syphilis Experiment",
      "text": "From 1946 to 1948, the U.S. government conducted experiments in Guatemala where doctors infected soldiers, prisoners, and mental patients with syphilis and other sexually transmitted diseases without their consent.",
