      "text": "In 1917, during World War I, the U.S. Navy established Naval Station Norfolk, which became the largest naval base in the world.",
      "date": "1917"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Desegregation of Public Schools",
      "text": "In 1959, Norfolk's public schools were desegregated following the Supreme Court's ruling in Brown v. Board of Education, marking a significant moment in the Civil Rights Movement.",
      "date": "1959"
