      "text": "In 1945, John von Neumann wrote the 'First Draft of a Report on the EDVAC', which laid out the design for a stored-program computer. This document became the foundation for the von Neumann architecture.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Components of the von Neumann Architecture",
      "text": "The von Neumann architecture describes a computer design with a processing unit containing an arithmetic logic unit and processor registers, a control unit with an instruction register and program counter, memory to store data and instructions, external mass storage, and input/output mechanisms.",
      "date": "1945"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Influence on Modern Computing",
      "text": "The von Neumann architecture has influenced the design of most modern computers, which typically follow this architecture or its derivatives.",
      "date": "1945"
