      "text": "Haji Bektash Veli, a key figure in Alevism, was born around 1209 in Nishapur, Khorasan, in present-day Iran.",
      "date": "1209"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Haji Bektash Veli's Migration to Anatolia",
      "text": "In the mid-13th century, Haji Bektash Veli migrated to Anatolia, where he began to spread his teachings, which would later form the basis of Alevism.",
      "date": "1250"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Haji Bektash Veli",
      "text": "Haji Bektash Veli passed away in 1271 in Anatolia. His teachings continued to influence the development of Alevism.",
      "date": "1271"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Bektashi Order",
      "text": "The Bektashi Order, a Sufi order closely associated with Alevism, was formally established in the late 13th century, following the death of Haji Bektash Veli.",
      "date": "1290"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Ottoman Recognition and Repression",
      "text": "During the Ottoman Empire, Alevis faced periods of both recognition and repression. The Bektashi Order was initially favored by the Janissaries but faced suppression after the abolition of the Janissaries in 1826.",
      "date": "1826"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Abolition of the Janissaries",
      "text": "In 1826, the Ottoman Sultan Mahmud II abolished the Janissary corps, which led to the suppression of the Bektashi Order, impacting Alevism.",
      "date": "1826"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Republic of Turkey and Secular Reforms",
      "text": "Following the establishment of the Republic of Turkey in 1923, secular reforms were implemented, which affected religious communities, including Alevis.",
      "date": "1923"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Alevi Massacres and Discrimination",
      "text": "Throughout the 20th century, Alevis in Turkey faced discrimination and violence, including the Maraş massacre in 1978 and the Sivas massacre in 1993.",
      "date": "1978"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sivas Massacre",
      "text": "On July 2, 1993, a mob set fire to a hotel in Sivas, Turkey, killing 37 people, mostly Alevis, during a cultural festival.",
      "date": "1993-07-02"
    }
  ]
}

