    },
    {
      "headline": "Post-War Education Reforms",
      "text": "Following World War II, significant education reforms were implemented, including the introduction of a 6-3-3-4 system (6 years of elementary, 3 years of lower secondary, 3 years of upper secondary, and 4 years of university).",
      "date": "1947"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology (MEXT)",
      "text": "The Ministry of Education was reorganized to become the Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology (MEXT), reflecting its expanded responsibilities.",
