    {
      "headline": "Start of Riots in England and Northern Ireland",
      "text": "From 30 July 2024, far-right, anti-immigration protests and riots began in England and Northern Ireland. These were fueled by false claims that the perpetrator of the Southport attack was a Muslim and an asylum seeker.",
      "date": "2024-07-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Continuation of Riots",
      "text": "The riots continued through to 5 August 2024, involving racist attacks, arson, and looting. This was the largest incident of social unrest in England since 2011.",
      "date": "2024-08-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sentencing of Rioters",
      "text": "By 8 August 2024, at least 200 people had been sentenced in relation to the riots, with 177 imprisoned. The average sentence was around two years, with some sentences reaching up to nine years.",
      "date": "2024-08-08"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Arrests and Charges",
      "text": "As of 1 September 2024, 1,280 arrests and nearly 800 charges had been made in connection with the unrest.",
