      "headline": "Coup Attempt by the 30 September Movement",
      "text": "On 1965-09-30, a group of Indonesian National Armed Forces members, known as the 30 September Movement, attempted a coup d'état, which led to the assassination of six Indonesian Army generals.",
      "date": "1965-09-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Suharto Takes Control",
      "text": "In the aftermath of the coup attempt, Major General Suharto quickly took control of the army and began a campaign against the Communist Party of Indonesia (PKI) and its sympathizers.",
      "date": "1965-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mass Killings Begin",
      "text": "Starting in October 1965, mass killings of alleged communists and sympathizers began across Indonesia. The violence was particularly intense in Java and Bali.",
      "date": "1965-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Foreign Support",
      "text": "Throughout the killings, the Indonesian authorities received support from foreign countries, including the United States and the United Kingdom, which provided intelligence and other assistance.",
      "date": "1965"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Mass Killings Continue",
      "text": "The mass killings continued into 1966, with estimates of the death toll ranging from 500,000 to 1 million people, with some estimates as high as two to three million.",
      "date": "1966"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Suharto's Rise to Power",
      "text": "By March 1966, Suharto had effectively taken control of the Indonesian government, marking the beginning of the New Order regime.",
      "date": "1966-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Mass Killings",
      "text": "The mass killings gradually subsided by the end of 1966, as Suharto consolidated his power and the PKI was effectively destroyed.",
      "date": "1966"
    }
  ]
}

