      "headline": "Control of Drug Trafficking in Mexico",
      "text": "Throughout the 1980s, the Guadalajara Cartel controlled much of the drug trafficking in Mexico and the corridors along the Mexico–United States border.",
      "date": "1980s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Expansion of Operations",
      "text": "The cartel expanded its operations to various regions in Mexico, including the states of Jalisco, Baja California, Colima, Sonora, Chihuahua, and Sinaloa.",
      "date": "1980s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Disintegration of the Guadalajara Cartel",
      "text": "The Guadalajara Cartel eventually disintegrated, leading to the formation of multiple modern-day drug cartels such as the Tijuana, Juárez, and Sinaloa cartels, which originally started out as branches or 'plazas' of the Guadalajara Cartel.",
      "date": "1980s"
