      "text": "The Schmidt sting pain index was developed by entomologist Justin O. Schmidt. It is a pain scale rating the relative pain caused by different hymenopteran stings. Schmidt's work involved being stung by various species to create a comparative scale.",
      "date": "1983"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of the Schmidt Sting Pain Index",
      "text": "In 1983, Justin O. Schmidt published the initial version of the Schmidt sting pain index, which included a scale from 1 to 4, with descriptions of the pain associated with each level.",
      "date": "1983"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Further Research and Publications",
      "text": "Throughout the 1980s and 1990s, Schmidt continued his research on hymenopteran stings, publishing numerous papers and expanding the index to include more species and detailed descriptions.",
      "date": "1980s-1990s"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Sting of the Wild'",
      "text": "In 2016, Justin O. Schmidt published a book titled 'The Sting of the Wild,' which detailed his experiences and findings related to the pain of insect stings, including the Schmidt sting pain index.",
      "date": "2016"
    }
  ]
}

