      "headline": "Birth of Anne Brontë",
      "text": "Anne Brontë was born on January 17, 1820, in Thornton, West Yorkshire, England.",
      "date": "1820-01-17"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Anne's Mother",
      "text": "Anne's mother, Maria Branwell Brontë, died of cancer on September 15, 1821, leaving her and her siblings to be raised by their father and aunt.",
      "date": "1821-09-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Education at Cowan Bridge",
      "text": "In 1824, Anne, along with her sisters, attended the Clergy Daughters' School at Cowan Bridge, which later inspired the depiction of Lowood School in Charlotte Brontë's 'Jane Eyre'.",
      "date": "1824"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Anne's Return Home",
      "text": "Anne returned home from Cowan Bridge in 1825 after her sisters Maria and Elizabeth died of tuberculosis.",
      "date": "1825"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Anne Becomes a Governess",
      "text": "In 1839, Anne Brontë took her first position as a governess with the Ingham family at Blake Hall, Mirfield.",
      "date": "1839"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Second Governess Position",
      "text": "Anne began working as a governess for the Robinson family at Thorp Green Hall in 1840, a position she held until 1845.",
      "date": "1840"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of Poems by Currer, Ellis, and Acton Bell",
      "text": "In 1846, Anne and her sisters Charlotte and Emily published a collection of poems under the pseudonyms Currer, Ellis, and Acton Bell.",
      "date": "1846"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'Agnes Grey'",
      "text": "Anne Brontë's first novel, 'Agnes Grey', was published in December 1847, drawing on her experiences as a governess.",
      "date": "1847-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Publication of 'The Tenant of Wildfell Hall'",
      "text": "Anne's second novel, 'The Tenant of Wildfell Hall', was published in June 1848 and was an immediate success.",
      "date": "1848-06"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Branwell Brontë",
      "text": "Anne's brother, Branwell Brontë, died on September 24, 1848, after a prolonged illness.",
      "date": "1848-09-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Emily Brontë",
      "text": "Anne's sister, Emily Brontë, died of tuberculosis on December 19, 1848.",
      "date": "1848-12-19"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Anne Brontë",
      "text": "Anne Brontë died of tuberculosis on May 28, 1849, in Scarborough, North Yorkshire, England.",
