      "text": "The Romantic Ballet era began in the 1830s, characterized by themes of fantasy and the supernatural, with 'La Sylphide' premiering in 1832.",
      "date": "1832"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Russian Influence",
      "text": "Ballet was further developed in Russia in the late 19th century, with the establishment of the Imperial Ballet School in 1738 and the creation of iconic ballets like 'Swan Lake' (1877) and 'The Nutcracker' (1892).",
      "date": "1877"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of Ballets Russes",
