      "headline": "Introduction of the Extradition Bill",
      "text": "In February 2019, the Hong Kong government introduced a bill to amend the Fugitive Offenders Ordinance, which would allow extradition to jurisdictions with which Hong Kong does not have existing extradition agreements, including mainland China.",
      "date": "2019-02"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Major Protest",
      "text": "On March 31, 2019, the first major protest against the extradition bill took place, organized by the Civil Human Rights Front, with thousands of participants.",
      "date": "2019-03-31"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Massive Protest on June 9",
      "text": "On June 9, 2019, over a million people marched in Hong Kong to protest against the extradition bill, marking one of the largest protests in the city's history.",
      "date": "2019-06-09"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Protest Escalation and Police Clashes",
      "text": "On June 12, 2019, protests escalated as demonstrators clashed with police outside the Legislative Council Complex, leading to the use of tear gas and rubber bullets by police.",
      "date": "2019-06-12"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Suspension of the Extradition Bill",
      "text": "On June 15, 2019, Hong Kong Chief Executive Carrie Lam announced the suspension of the extradition bill, but protests continued as demonstrators demanded a full withdrawal.",
      "date": "2019-06-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Storming of the Legislative Council",
      "text": "On July 1, 2019, protesters stormed and vandalized the Legislative Council building during the annual July 1 march, which commemorates the handover of Hong Kong to China.",
      "date": "2019-07-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "General Strike and Airport Protests",
      "text": "On August 5, 2019, a citywide general strike took place, and protests spread to Hong Kong International Airport, causing significant disruptions.",
      "date": "2019-08-05"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formal Withdrawal of the Extradition Bill",
      "text": "On September 4, 2019, Carrie Lam formally withdrew the extradition bill, but protests continued with broader demands for democratic reforms.",
      "date": "2019-09-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "District Council Elections",
      "text": "On November 24, 2019, pro-democracy candidates won a landslide victory in the District Council elections, gaining control of 17 out of 18 councils.",
      "date": "2019-11-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "COVID-19 Pandemic Impact",
      "text": "In early 2020, the COVID-19 pandemic led to a decrease in protest activities due to health concerns and restrictions on gatherings.",
      "date": "2020"
    }
  ]
}

