      "headline": "Strategic Arms Limitation Talks (SALT I)",
      "text": "In 1972, the United States and the Soviet Union signed the Strategic Arms Limitation Talks (SALT I) agreement, marking a significant step in the détente process by limiting the number of nuclear weapons.",
      "date": "1972"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Helsinki Accords",
      "text": "In 1975, the Helsinki Accords were signed by 35 nations, including the United States and the Soviet Union, to improve relations between the Communist bloc and the West.",
      "date": "1975"
    },
    {
      "headline": "End of Détente",
      "text": "Détente effectively ended in the late 1970s and early 1980s due to renewed tensions, including the Soviet invasion of Afghanistan in 1979 and the election of Ronald Reagan as U.S. President in 1980, who took a more hardline stance against the Soviet Union.",
      "date": "1980"
    }
  ]
}

