      "headline": "U.S. Supreme Court Decision",
      "text": "On June 13, 1966, the U.S. Supreme Court issued its decision in Miranda v. Arizona, ruling that the Fifth Amendment requires that individuals be informed of their rights before police interrogation.",
      "date": "1966-06-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Establishment of Miranda Rights",
      "text": "The Supreme Court's decision established the 'Miranda Rights,' requiring law enforcement to inform detainees of their rights to silence and legal counsel.",
      "date": "1966-06-13"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Retrial and Conviction",
      "text": "Ernesto Miranda was retried without his confession being used as evidence and was convicted again in 1967.",
      "date": "1967"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Miranda's Release",
      "text": "Miranda was paroled in 1972 after serving 11 years in prison.",
      "date": "1972"
    },
