      "text": "Guan Yu was born in the late Eastern Han dynasty, but the exact date of his birth is not recorded. He is believed to have been born around the year 160.",
      "date": "0160"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Service under Liu Bei",
      "text": "Guan Yu began serving under the warlord Liu Bei, forming a brotherly bond with him and Zhang Fei. This relationship played a significant role in his life and career.",
      "date": "0180"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Boma",
      "text": "In 200, Guan Yu repaid Cao Cao's kindness by slaying Yan Liang, a general under Cao Cao's rival Yuan Shao, at the Battle of Boma.",
      "date": "0200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Governing Jing Province",
      "text": "After Liu Bei gained control of Yi Province in 214, Guan Yu remained in Jing Province to govern and defend the area for about seven years.",
      "date": "0214"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Fancheng",
      "text": "In 219, Guan Yu fought Cao Cao's forces at the Battle of Fancheng. During this time, Sun Quan broke the Sun–Liu alliance and sent his general Lü Meng to conquer Liu Bei's territories in Jing Province.",
      "date": "0219"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Capture and Execution",
      "text": "After his defeat at Fancheng and the loss of Jing Province, Guan Yu was captured in an ambush by Sun Quan's forces and executed at Linju, Xiangyang Commandery in 219.",
