      "headline": "Matthias Schleiden's Contribution",
      "text": "In 1838, Matthias Schleiden, a German botanist, concluded that all plant tissues are composed of cells and that an embryonic plant always arises from a single cell.",
      "date": "1838"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Theodor Schwann's Contribution",
      "text": "In 1839, Theodor Schwann, a German physiologist, extended Schleiden's cell theory to animals, stating that all living things are composed of cells.",
      "date": "1839"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Rudolf Virchow's Addition",
      "text": "In 1855, Rudolf Virchow, a German physician, added to the cell theory by stating 'Omnis cellula e cellula', meaning all cells arise from pre-existing cells.",
      "date": "1855"
    }
  ]
}

