      "headline": "Indian Independence Act 1947",
      "text": "The Indian Independence Act 1947 was passed by the British Parliament, which led to the creation of the independent dominions of India and Pakistan. This act came into effect on 15 August 1947.",
      "date": "1947-08-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Formation of the Dominion of India",
      "text": "On 15 August 1947, the Dominion of India was established as an independent dominion within the British Commonwealth of Nations. It marked the end of British rule in India.",
      "date": "1947-08-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Partition of British India",
      "text": "The partition of British India into two independent dominions, India and Pakistan, took place on 15 August 1947. This led to significant demographic changes and mass migrations.",
      "date": "1947-08-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Integration of Princely States",
      "text": "Following independence, the princely states were advised to join either India or Pakistan. Most states acceded to India, significantly shaping the political landscape of the new dominion.",
      "date": "1947-1949"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Adoption of the Constitution of India",
      "text": "The Constitution of India was adopted on 26 November 1949, laying the foundation for the Republic of India.",
      "date": "1949-11-26"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Transition to Republic of India",
      "text": "On 26 January 1950, the Dominion of India became the Republic of India, marking the end of the dominion status and the establishment of a sovereign republic.",
      "date": "1950-01-26"
    }
  ]
}

