      "headline": "Creation of Lupin III",
      "text": "The original Lupin III manga began serialization in Weekly Manga Action on August 10, 1967. Created by Monkey Punch, the series follows the adventures of master thief Lupin III, the grandson of the fictional gentleman thief Arsène Lupin.",
      "date": "1967-08-10"
    },
    {
      "headline": "First Lupin III Anime Series",
      "text": "The first Lupin III anime series, known as 'Lupin III Part I' or 'The Classic Adventures,' aired from October 24, 1971, to March 26, 1972. It introduced the characters to a broader audience and established the franchise's popularity.",
      "date": "1971-10-24"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Release of 'The Castle of Cagliostro'",
      "text": "On December 15, 1979, 'The Castle of Cagliostro,' a feature film directed by Hayao Miyazaki, was released. It is one of the most acclaimed entries in the Lupin III franchise and is notable for its influence on the animation industry.",
      "date": "1979-12-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lupin III Part II",
      "text": "The second Lupin III anime series, known as 'Lupin III Part II' or 'Shin Lupin III,' aired from October 3, 1977, to October 6, 1980. It further expanded the adventures of Lupin and his gang.",
      "date": "1977-10-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lupin III Part III",
      "text": "The third anime series, 'Lupin III Part III,' aired from March 3, 1984, to November 6, 1985. It continued the tradition of Lupin's escapades with a new art style and tone.",
      "date": "1984-03-03"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lupin III Part IV",
      "text": "The fourth anime series, 'Lupin III Part IV: The Italian Adventure,' premiered on August 30, 2015, in Italy and on October 1, 2015, in Japan. It marked a return to the classic style and was set primarily in Italy.",
      "date": "2015-08-30"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lupin III Part V",
      "text": "The fifth anime series, 'Lupin III Part V: Misadventures in France,' aired from April 4, 2018, to September 18, 2018. It brought Lupin into the digital age, exploring themes of technology and privacy.",
      "date": "2018-04-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Lupin III Part VI",
      "text": "The sixth anime series, 'Lupin III Part VI,' began airing on October 10, 2021, celebrating the 50th anniversary of the Lupin III anime. It features new adventures and mysteries for Lupin and his gang.",
      "date": "2021-10-10"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "timeline": [
    {
      "headline": "Birth of Cao Cao",
      "text": "Cao Cao was born in 155 in Qiao County, Pei Commandery, which is present-day Bozhou, Anhui.",
      "date": "0155"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cao Cao's Early Career",
      "text": "In 175, Cao Cao was appointed as a district captain of Luoyang, the capital of the Eastern Han dynasty.",
      "date": "0175"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cao Cao's Role in Suppressing the Yellow Turban Rebellion",
      "text": "In 184, Cao Cao participated in the suppression of the Yellow Turban Rebellion, a peasant uprising that threatened the Han dynasty.",
      "date": "0184"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cao Cao's Rise to Power",
      "text": "In 189, following the death of Emperor Ling, Cao Cao joined the coalition against the warlord Dong Zhuo, who had taken control of the Han central government.",
      "date": "0189"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Guandu",
      "text": "In 200, Cao Cao achieved a decisive victory over the warlord Yuan Shao at the Battle of Guandu, solidifying his power in northern China.",
      "date": "0200"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Battle of Red Cliffs",
      "text": "In 208, Cao Cao faced a major defeat at the Battle of Red Cliffs against the allied forces of Sun Quan and Liu Bei, which prevented him from unifying southern China.",
      "date": "0208"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Creation of the State of Cao Wei",
      "text": "In 213, Cao Cao was granted the title of Duke of Wei, and in 216, he was promoted to King of Wei, laying the foundation for the state of Cao Wei.",
      "date": "0216"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Cao Cao",
      "text": "Cao Cao died on March 15, 220, in Luoyang, Henan. His death marked the end of his control over the Han central government.",
      "date": "0220-03-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Posthumous Events",
      "text": "Later in 220, Cao Cao's son, Cao Pi, declared himself emperor, ending the Han dynasty and establishing the state of Cao Wei, thus beginning the Three Kingdoms period.",
      "date": "0220"
    }
  ]
}

