      "headline": "Development of the Axiom of Choice",
      "text": "The Banach–Tarski paradox relies heavily on the Axiom of Choice, a controversial principle in set theory that was developed in the early 20th century. This axiom allows for the selection of elements from an infinite number of sets.",
      "date": "Early 20th century"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Impact on Mathematics",
      "text": "The Banach–Tarski paradox has had a significant impact on the field of mathematics, particularly in the areas of set theory and geometry. It has sparked discussions and debates regarding the nature of infinity and the foundations of mathematics.",
