    {
      "headline": "Declaration of the Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus",
      "text": "On November 15, 1983, the Turkish Republic of Northern Cyprus (TRNC) was unilaterally declared, recognized only by Turkey.",
      "date": "1983-11-15"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Cyprus Joins the European Union",
      "text": "On May 1, 2004, the Republic of Cyprus joined the European Union, although the acquis communautaire is suspended in the northern part of the island.",
      "date": "2004-05-01"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Annan Plan Referendum",
      "text": "In April 2004, a United Nations-backed plan to reunify Cyprus, known as the Annan Plan, was put to a referendum. It was accepted by Turkish Cypriots but rejected by Greek Cypriots.",
      "date": "2004-04"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Crans-Montana Talks",
